      },
      "text": "Severe weather requires three ingredients: instability (CAPE), moisture, and wind shear. The wind shear component — both speed shear and directional shear — is what separates ordinary thunderstorms from organized, long-lived severe weather systems."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-SEVERE-WEATHER.md#003",
