        "title": "Severe Weather - Supercells, Tornadoes, Tropical Cyclones",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Multiple cells arranged in a line (cold front, dryline, or outflow boundary). New cells form on the flank:\n- **Squall line** = organized linear MCS (Mesoscale Convective System)\n- **QLCS** = Quasi-Linear Convective System; can produce tornadoes (brief, embedded)\n- Typical severe weather: large hail, strong winds (derecho potential), heavy rain"
