        "current_path": "meteorology/06-SEVERE-WEATHER.md",
        "id": "maxim:meteorology:severe-weather",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "meteorology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[severe, weather]",
        "section": "meteorology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Severe Weather - Supercells, Tornadoes, Tropical Cyclones",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TORNADO STRUCTURE:\n  Wall cloud → Rotating contact → Funnel cloud → Dust whirl → Condensation funnel\n  (funnel appears as condensation where adiabatic cooling reaches the dewpoint;\n   the tornado itself extends even when funnel isn't visible)\n```"
    },
    {
