        "root_concepts": "[severe, weather]",
        "section": "meteorology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Severe Weather - Supercells, Tornadoes, Tropical Cyclones",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MECHANISM:\n  Squall line develops strong rear-inflow jet at mid-levels\n  → Descends to surface → \"bow echo\" on radar\n  → Straight-line damage (not rotating like tornado)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-SEVERE-WEATHER.md#037",
      "path": [
        "06-SEVERE-WEATHER.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
